Snow-17: fortran/snow17_shim.f90 links directly against the unmodified
FORTRAN-77 physics files in external/snow17/src/snow19/ (vendored as a
git submodule, pinned to a specific commit -- see external/snow17's own
commit hash for the exact version and its known issues). No changes were
made to any snow19/ source file; the shim only adds a bind(C) driver loop
around EXSNOW19.

SAC-SMA: fortran/sacsma_shim.f90 links against external/sac-sma/src/sac/
(vendored as a git submodule, pinned to a specific commit). One disclosed,
minimal patch is applied to a build-time-only copy of src/sac/sac1.f90 --
see patches/sac1_bypass_ratio_check_save_fix.patch and notes/NOTES.md for
the confirmed upstream defect it fixes (a local variable's Fortran-
mandated implicit SAVE attribute causing state to silently leak between
calls). external/sac-sma itself is never modified; `git submodule status`
stays byte-identical to the pinned upstream commit. The shim otherwise
only adds a bind(C) driver loop around EXSAC.

See https://github.com/NOAA-OWP/snow17/blob/main/LICENSE and
https://github.com/NOAA-OWP/sac-sma/blob/main/LICENSE for the full
upstream license texts (both Apache-2.0).
